    </div>

    <div class="takeaway">
      <strong>3. Entire-home dominance signals commercialization.</strong> {top3_entire.index[0]} ({fmt_pct(top3_entire.values[0])}), {top3_entire.index[1]} ({fmt_pct(top3_entire.values[1])}), and {top3_entire.index[2]} ({fmt_pct(top3_entire.values[2])}) have the highest entire-home shares. Markets where entire-home listings predominate tend to have more professional operators and face greater regulatory scrutiny — policymakers often target entire-home listings when tightening short-term rental rules.
    </div>

    <div class="takeaway">
      <strong>4. {highest_rpm} leads in review activity (avg {avg_rpm[highest_rpm]:.2f} reviews/month),</strong> indicating strong and recurring guest demand. High review frequency combined with high availability suggests a mature, high-throughput market. Cities with lower review rates may represent underpenetrated markets or ones where guests book through alternative channels.
    </div>

    <div class="takeaway">
